# --- Operator-private / local-only material: never enters this public repo ---
#
# `local` is a symlink to the private layer (the privacy pattern list, lab topology, personal
# transcripts). Every clone that can run a privacy sweep has to create it — `ln -s <private> local`
# — so the tooling for the check mandates an artifact in the working tree, and without this file a
# single `git add -A` commits an absolute path to the Operator's machine into a public repository.
#
# That is not hypothetical: it happened on quince-devlog#28 and was caught in review rather than by
# the sweep, which reported CLEAN on a diff containing the path — the pattern list cannot match a
# path created the same day. `quince` has carried `/local` since qn.0; this repo never had a
# .gitignore at all, which is why the same symlink is invisible there and staged-in-waiting here.
/local

# Claude Code machine-local settings (the shared settings.json is tracked where one exists).
/.claude/settings.local.json
